# Overall assessment: Yes, this is a genuinely promising research project.

Having reviewed both documents, my recommendation is to pursue the idea as a research project, not merely as an AutoSE course assignment.

The central hypothesis is interesting:

> Instead of teaching a small language model to write a formal proof, can we get better verified programs by teaching it to write implementations that are easier for a theorem prover to verify automatically?

This is a meaningful shift in how we allocate work between an LLM and a formal verification system.

