## 5. The research design I would ultimately recommend

I would consolidate the two documents into this design.

## Proposed experimental framework

PRIMARY EXPERIMENT

A. Single-shot baseline

Model generates implementation and proof independently. Measure pass\@N.

B. Feedback-guided proof-writing

Model iteratively repairs implementation and proof using Lean feedback.

C. Automation-friendly repair

Model repairs implementation only. Fixed Lean tactics attempt to prove it. Structural hints are provided when necessary.

ABLATIONS AND CONTROLS

C-plain

Code-only model with no meaningful structural hint, to measure the contribution of structured feedback.

T. Fixed automation reference

Run the same tactic portfolio on buggy and correct reference implementations. Establish its existing coverage.

MECHANISM STUDY

Proofability under equivalent implementations

Study which semantics-preserving implementation transformations improve automated proof success.

### Research questions

I would use these four:

RQ1 – Effectiveness: Does automation-friendly program repair achieve a higher end-to-end verified repair rate than feedback-guided proof-writing under matched computational budgets?

RQ2 – Mechanism: Which implementation transformations and defect categories contribute most to automation-friendly repair success?

RQ3 – Feedback: Does providing structured Lean proof-obligation feedback improve repair performance compared with simple retry feedback?

RQ4 – Engineering trade-offs: What are the differences in runtime, model tokens, patch size, code complexity, behavioural regressions, and specification-gaming attempts?

This combines the strongest aspects of both PDFs without overloading the project with too many research questions.

### Models and dataset

I would preserve your original choices:

| Component          | Recommendation                                             |
| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| Models             | Qwen2.5-Coder 1.5B and 3B Instruct                         |
| Quantization       | 4-bit                                                      |
| Main benchmark     | VERINA                                                     |
| Task construction  | Controlled mutations                                       |
| Validation         | Naturally generated faulty implementations                 |
| Main conditions    | A, B, C                                                    |
