### Hardware feasibility

Your primary model choices are sensible for a low-resource experiment. The project does not require training or fine-tuning, which keeps the computational burden manageable.

Your RTX 4050 6GB laptop is a reasonable starting point for the 1.5B and 3B models at 4-bit quantization. Your 16GB system RAM is at the minimum specified in the proposal, though Lean and Mathlib can be memory-intensive. I would avoid making the optional 7B model a dependency for project completion.

Use `llama.cpp` for the local inference setup, measure actual VRAM and RAM usage, and initially keep Lean verification parallelism conservative.&#x20;

