### My three most important recommendations

1\. Do not change the central idea. The code-only repair versus model-written proof comparison is worth investigating. It is the most compelling part of the project.

2\. Add the proofability mechanism experiment. This is my biggest recommendation. It can turn the work from a comparison of two prompting strategies into a deeper study of how implementation structure affects automated verification.

3\. Make the experimental protocol stricter than the proposal currently specifies. In particular, fix the budget definition, benchmark construction, hidden-test methodology, and the differences between the two PDFs.

My preferred final title would remain:

Prove Less, Repair Better: Automation-Friendly Program Repair for Small Models in Lean 4

It is memorable, communicates the main idea, and is appropriate for the intended research community.

My overall advice: Proceed with this project. Do not treat the course grade as the endpoint. Treat the seven-week project as the first stage of a longer research effort, with a proper publication as the objective.

The most useful next deliverable is a single, reconciled research protocol and updated novelty matrix that incorporates the newer literature before the team freezes its experimental design.